  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot {[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
